@startuml
actor "User" as User
participant ":Search Page\n(Frontend)" as UI
participant ":PipelineStore\n(Zustand)" as Store
participant ":API Gateway\n(/search)" as API
participant ":ProjectService" as PS
participant ":ProjectRepository" as PR
participant ":SearchService" as SS
participant ":DocumentRepository" as DR

autonumber

== Preconditions ==
note over User, UI
  User is authenticated. A project may or may not be active
  (project context is only required to resolve project-scoped subtopics).
end note

== Main Flow ==

User -> UI : Navigate to Search page
UI -> Store : Load pipeline state (project_id)
Store --> UI : Restore state (if any pending_pipeline)

User -> UI : Input search parameters\n(keywords, date range, languages,\nplatforms, topics, subtopics,\nconfidence_threshold)
User -> UI : Trigger search

UI -> API : POST /search/?project_id={id}\n{ SearchQuery }
API -> API : get_current_user (verify bearer token)

opt query.subtopics AND project_id provided
    API -> PS : verify_project_owner(project_id, user_id)
    PS -> PR : find_by_id(project_id)
    PR --> PS : Project | None
    alt project missing or not owned
        PS --> API : raise ProjectNotFound / ProjectAccessDenied
        API --> UI : 404 Not Found / 403 Access denied
    end
    API -> PS : filter_proxies_by_subtopics\n(project_id, subtopics, confidence_threshold)
    PS -> PR : filter_proxy_doc_ids_by_subtopics\n(project_id, subtopics, confidence_threshold)
    PR --> PS : dict { doc_id -> [matched subtopic names] }
    PS --> API : proxy_subtopics
end

API -> SS : search(SearchQuery,\nproxy_doc_ids = list(proxy_subtopics))
SS -> DR : find(SearchQuery, proxy_doc_ids)
note right of DR
  proxy_doc_ids are folded into the subtopic $or clause:
  a document matches a subtopic via documents.subtopics
  (db-native) OR by being one of the project's proxy ids.
  Union, not a narrowing second pass.
end note
DR --> SS : list[Document]
SS -> DR : count(SearchQuery, proxy_doc_ids)
DR --> SS : int
SS --> API : SearchResult\n(total_docs, list[DocumentSummary])

opt proxy_subtopics not empty
    API -> API : Enrich each matched DocumentSummary.relevant_topics\nwith its project subtopic names
end

API --> UI : 200 OK — SearchResult

alt total_docs > 0
    UI -> Store : Save SearchResult + SearchQuery\nMark search step complete
    Store --> UI : Pipeline step "Generate Topics" unlocked
    UI --> User : Display total document count\n+ list of DocumentSummary\n(headline, excerpt, platform, language, date, relevant_topics)
else No documents found
    UI --> User : Informational message: no documents matched\nthe parameters (not an error). Pipeline steps stay locked.
end

note over UI, API
  Search without a project_id (or without subtopics) skips the
  ProjectService/ProjectRepository calls entirely. Subtopics are then
  matched only against db-native documents.subtopics; project-exclusive
  subtopics are not resolvable without project context.
end note

@enduml
